<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    RM_LeaningScrub_Biome.xml                  LEANINGSCRUB_RM_MOD_BUILD_1

    Phase A row 9 of design/RimMandrake/biome_mod_architecture.md — the
    RimMandrake-tier twin of the frozen src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/Defs/
    BiomeDefs/RUT_AridShrubland.xml, generalized to zero campaign-specific
    content per §3a's test. Full sheet (campaign-side):
    design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/arid_shrubland.md (FROZEN).

    Copied from the frozen def, MEASURED 2026-09-25: terrain thresholds,
    weather commonalities, disease table and animalDensity/plantDensity/
    forageability/movementDifficulty/diseaseMtbDays/wildPlantRegrowDays are
    all byte-identical to RUT_AridShrubland.xml's own values — nothing here
    is re-derived. workerClass stays RimWorld.BiomeWorker_AridShrubland
    (vanilla Core, confirmed via the installed game's own
    Biomes_WarmArid.xml) — a donor type in workerClass would be a hard
    dependency the RimMandrake tier may not assume, but this one is Core
    itself, so no RM_BiomeWorker_LeaningScrub wrapper is owed.

    <texture> is vanilla Core's own "World/Biomes/AridShrubland" (MEASURED
    from Biomes_WarmArid.xml on the installed game), NOT the frozen twin's
    "World/Biomes/AridShrubland1" — that suffixed variant belongs to a
    Workshop donor mod (id 3546956014), and this mod ships standalone.

    wildAnimals: every RSW_/SW_/donor-Star-Wars-name entry stays OUT (per
    §7 Q11, "RimMandrake should not name star wars ever") and rides
    src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/Patches/WildAnimals_LeaningScrub.xml
    instead. Only the 5 non-Star-Wars rows the frozen def already carries
    are inline here (Q9: non-Star-Wars donor fauna is acceptable inline).

    wildPlants: the frozen def's own RUT_-prefixed plant defs (RUT_Fuzz,
    RUT_Grellbush, RUT_Grellspine, RUT_WildHealroot, RUT_SweetlineTree,
    formerly mandrake.rut.ashkarrflora) are renamed to this mod's RM_ tier
    per §7 Q8 ("mandrake.rut.ashkarrflora: DISSOLVE IT. Each plant moves
    into the RimMandrake mod of the biome whose wildPlants lists it,
    renamed RM_"). 🔑 The ORIGINAL RUT_-prefixed defs are left standing,
    UNTOUCHED, inside mandrake.rut.ashkarrflora: the frozen
    RUT_AridShrubland.xml's own wildPlants block still names them under
    MayRequire="mandrake.rut.ashkarrflora", and that mod carries the
    player's live world until Phase B deletes RUT_AridShrubland.xml
    outright (biome_mod_architecture.md §5's hazard section — a defName a
    frozen def depends on cannot be pulled out from under it before then).
    So mandrake.rut.ashkarrflora is not literally dissolved THIS pass; it
    is frozen alongside its biome, exactly the same bounded-duplication
    pattern §5 step 3 already uses for the biome def itself, and its real
    deletion is scheduled for Phase B step 4 together with
    RUT_AridShrubland.xml. This is the one deliberate deviation from the
    item's literal "move" wording, made to avoid the exact hazard §5
    documents for biome defs, applied one level down to a def a frozen
    biome depends on.

    RG_Plant_AridGrass / Plant_Nysyllin_Wild / RG_Plant_CreepStern /
    RG_Plant_CrimsonCushion / RG_Plant_Dervish carry no MayRequire in the
    frozen def either — copied byte-identical; fixing that donor-gating gap
    is not this item's scope.

    Art: RM_Fuzz/RM_Grellbush/RM_Grellspine/RM_WildHealroot have zero PNGs
    anywhere (MEASURED, same as the frozen originals) — expected, not a
    defect (CLAUDE.md, "prove art is missing before generating"; the
    existing artpipe jobs target the OLD RUT_ texPaths inside
    mandrake.rut.ashkarrflora and do not benefit these new RM_ defs — a
    separate, later art-queue concern, not filed here). RM_SweetlineTree's
    14-variant art is copied and renamed alongside its def (see
    Textures/Things/Plant/RM_SweetlineTree/).
  -->

  <BiomeDef>
    <defName>RM_LeaningScrub</defName>
    <label>the leaning scrub</label>
    <description>Knee-high silver-green fuzz at eerily even spacing, running unbroken to every horizon, all of it leaning the same way, all of it moving - because the wind never stops. Sightlines are gone under the fuzz-canopy and cover is everywhere, for everything smaller than a person, all the time.</description>
    <workerClass>RimWorld.BiomeWorker_AridShrubland</workerClass>
    <texture>World/Biomes/AridShrubland</texture>
    <riverbankTerrain>Riverbank</riverbankTerrain>
    <allowRoads>true</allowRoads>
    <allowRivers>true</allowRivers>
    <allowFarmingCamps>false</allowFarmingCamps>
    <animalDensity>1.8</animalDensity>
    <plantDensity>0.35</plantDensity>
    <forageability>0.5</forageability>
    <movementDifficulty>1</movementDifficulty>
    <diseaseMtbDays>65</diseaseMtbDays>
    <diseases>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Flu</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Plague</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_GutWorms</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>60</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_MuscleParasites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>60</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_FibrousMechanites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>30</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_SensoryMechanites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>30</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_AnimalFlu</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_AnimalPlague</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_OrganDecay</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>10</commonality>
      </li>
    </diseases>
    <terrainsByFertility>
      <li>
        <terrain>Sand</terrain>
        <min>-999</min>
        <max>0.45</max>
      </li>
      <li>
        <terrain>Soil</terrain>
        <min>0.45</min>
        <max>0.9</max>
      </li>
      <li>
        <terrain>SoilRich</terrain>
        <min>0.9</min>
        <max>999</max>
      </li>
    </terrainsByFertility>
    <baseWeatherCommonalities>
      <Clear>30</Clear>
      <Fog>45</Fog>
      <DryThunderstorm>1</DryThunderstorm>
      <SnowGentle>0</SnowGentle>
      <SnowHard>0</SnowHard>
      <Rain>0</Rain>
      <RainyThunderstorm>0</RainyThunderstorm>
      <FoggyRain>0</FoggyRain>
      <GrayPall MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Anomaly">1</GrayPall>
      <Overcast MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">5</Overcast>
    </baseWeatherCommonalities>
    <wildAnimals>
      <Terrorworm MayRequire="mlie.horrors">0.7</Terrorworm>  <!-- terrorworm - non-Star-Wars donor, Q9 -->
      <AA_Cactipine MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.25</AA_Cactipine>  <!-- cactipine - non-Star-Wars donor, Q9 -->
      <AA_Needlepost MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.1</AA_Needlepost>  <!-- needlepost - non-Star-Wars donor, Q9 -->
      <AA_Wildpawn MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.1</AA_Wildpawn>  <!-- wildpawn - non-Star-Wars donor, Q9 -->
      <AA_Wildpod MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.025</AA_Wildpod>  <!-- wildpod - non-Star-Wars donor, Q9 -->
    </wildAnimals>
    <coastalWildAnimals />
    <wildPlants>
      <RM_Fuzz>0.9</RM_Fuzz>  <!-- LEANINGSCRUB_RM_MOD_BUILD_1: renamed from RUT_Fuzz, §7 Q8 -->
      <RG_Plant_AridGrass>0.5</RG_Plant_AridGrass>  <!-- grass -->
      <Plant_Brambles>0.3</Plant_Brambles>  <!-- brambles -->
      <RM_Grellbush>0.3</RM_Grellbush>  <!-- renamed from RUT_Grellbush, §7 Q8 -->
      <RM_Grellspine>0.3</RM_Grellspine>  <!-- renamed from RUT_Grellspine, §7 Q8 -->
      <RM_WildHealroot>0.25</RM_WildHealroot>  <!-- renamed from RUT_WildHealroot, §7 Q8; label kept "wild healroot" -->
      <Plant_Nysyllin_Wild>0.22</Plant_Nysyllin_Wild>  <!-- wild nysyllin plant; not IP per Q11a -->
      <RG_Plant_CreepStern>0.2</RG_Plant_CreepStern>  <!-- creep stern -->
      <RG_Plant_CrimsonCushion>0.2</RG_Plant_CrimsonCushion>  <!-- crimson cushion -->
      <RG_Plant_Dervish>0.2</RG_Plant_Dervish>  <!-- dervish -->
      <RM_VenomvineThicket MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">0.15</RM_VenomvineThicket>  <!-- fortress flora, already RimMandrake-tier, no move -->
    </wildPlants>
    <!-- RM_SweetlineTree (renamed from RUT_SweetlineTree, §7 Q8) ships as its own
         def in this mod (Defs/ThingDefs_Plants/RM_SweetlineTree.xml) but is
         deliberately NOT added to wildPlants above: the frozen twin never wired
         it into spawning either (0 references to it anywhere besides its own
         file, MEASURED) and TREE_GRAPHICS_OWNERSHIP_1 is still open on how the
         landmark tree should actually place (a hand-placed one-per-sweetline
         "living surveyor's mark", not a random wildPlants scatter, per its own
         design sheet). Inventing a commonality number here would be exactly the
         kind of data decision that item, not this one, owns. -->
    <wildPlantRegrowDays>27</wildPlantRegrowDays>
  </BiomeDef>

</Defs>
